{% comment %}
  Text-only desktop mega menu panel: every option is a named link, no picture tiles.

  Used by the menus 'menu-static-layout' returns "links" for, which is now all of them. Three
  regions on every menu; what each menu puts in them is set in the case block below:
  - Browse (left): the menu's own groups side by side as columns of links, and then any
    row-style group full width underneath. The style column carries a picture from the theme's
    assets beside each name, and the other icon columns a line drawing ('menu-link-icon' holds
    which file each name takes and what it falls back to). Only Engagement ends
    its columns with the shared guide pages; the other menus give that room to their own
    options, and Diamonds has its own "Learn" column of guides.
  - Promo (right): a heading over a picture, which is inset from the right edge of the panel
    and carries a line of copy and two entry points over its foot. Engagement and Diamonds
    show the Design Studio there, Wedding and Jewellery a collection. The heading takes the
    same rule as the browse columns, so they all line up across the panel.
  - Footer: a hairline strip across both carrying the menu's "View all".

  Accepts:
  - link: {Object} the top-level menu link
  - drawer_id: {String}

  The lists themselves all come from 'menu-static-items', so the names here cannot drift apart
  from the menu; this snippet only decides which groups a menu draws, in what order and how wide
  each one runs. Columns are declared per menu in `browse_columns` below as

      group|Heading|styles|heading-url

  - group is the name 'menu-static-items' lists the items under; "Guides" is the shared list of
    guide pages, which any menu can ask for.
  - Heading defaults to the group's own name.
  - styles is a space-separated list, any of: "split" for a long list in two sub-columns,
    "compact" for a narrower column, which is what lets a menu run five of them in one row,
    "inline" for a row of links that runs full width under the columns, and one of the four
    icon sets - "shapes" for the cut drawings from 'icon-diamond-shape', "ring-styles" for the
    setting pictures in assets, "types" for the piece drawings from
    'icon-jewellery-type', "stones" for the material drawings from 'icon-stone'. Blank is a
    plain single column with no drawings. Only a list whose every name is drawn in that set may
    ask for it, or the names it misses would each carry an empty box.
  - heading-url is optional and gives the column a "View all" link under its names, for a
    group that is also a collection. The heading itself is never a link: one destination per
    column, in one place.

  Order matters: a column is drawn where it is listed, so the "inline" rows go last.
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign parent_key = link.title | handle

  comment
    Defaults, for a menu that asks for this panel without being named below: its own groups are
    not known here, so it gets the guide pages and the studio alone rather than an empty half.
  endcomment
  assign browse_columns = 'Guides|Guides|' | split: ','
  assign parent_lower = link.title | downcase
  assign view_all_label = 'View all ' | append: parent_lower

  comment
    The promo picture that fills the right-hand half. Every one of them is a portrait asset
    under assets/, framed by the half rather than by its own proportions, and it sits behind
    the words carrying nothing they do not - so it goes in decorative, alt="", rather than a
    description a screen reader would read out over the heading.

    'promo_style' is the modifier the picture takes: "studio" holds the workshop bench just
    below centre, where the collection pictures are framed on the piece and want none.
  endcomment
  assign promo_heading = 'Design Studio'
  assign promo_url = '/pages/design-studio'
  assign promo_image = 'about-craft-workshop.png'
  assign promo_width = 1086
  assign promo_height = 1448
  assign promo_style = 'studio'
  assign promo_text = 'Have a piece made to your own design, or ask us to remake something you love.'
  assign promo_actions = 'Explore the studio|/pages/design-studio,Talk to a designer|/pages/contact' | split: ','

  comment
    An optional second picture, standing beside the promo in the same half as
    'Name|url|asset|width|height'. Only a menu whose browse columns stop well short of the
    picture asks for one - Wedding, whose four capped columns leave about a fifth of the panel
    empty between the names and the promo - and the CSS draws it only on the wide screens where
    that room exists. Blank is one picture, which is every other menu.
  endcomment
  assign promo_secondary = ''

  comment
    Metal is deliberately absent from Engagement: it is a filter on the collection page, and as a
    third column beside the two long ones it left a ragged row. Wedding, whose lists are short,
    gives it a column of its own.

    Every studio action has to land somewhere that exists: the builder page is the setting-first
    route ('design-studio-builder'), and the designer route is the bespoke enquiry page. 'Label|url'
    each, and the two of them are what sits over the foot of the picture.
  endcomment
  case parent_key
    when 'engagement'
      assign browse_columns = 'By Style|Shop by Style|ring-styles split,By Shape|Shop by Shape|shapes split,Guides|Guides|' | split: ','
      assign view_all_label = 'View all engagement rings'
      assign promo_text = 'Build a ring from the setting up, or start from the stone and let us set it.'
      assign promo_actions = 'Create your own design|/pages/design-studio-builder,Talk to our designer|/pages/bespoke-jewellery-request' | split: ','
    when 'wedding'
      comment
        Four columns, where there were three. Three lists of four short names left the browse half
        about 22rem tall against a promo picture that floors at 30rem, so the panel carried a band
        of empty white under the names; the shared Guides list is the longest column the menu can
        ask for and it anchors the row at the height the picture sets.

        By Style carries a line drawing of the band itself beside each name, one per style
        ('band-style-<handle>.png', see 'menu-link-icon'), which gives these names
        the same visual weight as Engagement's picture-led styles. Drawings rather than the tile
        photographs the mobile menu shows: at icon size a photograph of a plain band and a
        photograph of a pavé one are the same grey ellipse, where the drawings say in one look
        how much of each band is set. The set is 'band-styles', not 'ring-styles': none of these
        four is a setting, and 'icon-ring-style' draws nothing for them.

        No Shape column here. The cuts are Engagement's browse axis and the wedding range carries
        no shape tag at all - every cut under this menu would open an empty filter.

        The headings are the short forms - "By Style", not "Shop by Style" - and the columns are
        compact, both for the same reason Jewellery's five are: at the narrow end of the desktop
        range a quarter of the browse half is about 13rem, which "Shop by Style" overruns, and a
        heading that wraps takes its rule out of line with the three beside it.
      endcomment
      assign browse_columns = 'By Style|By Style|band-styles compact,Featured|Featured|compact,By Metal|By Metal|compact,Guides|Guides|compact' | split: ','
      assign view_all_label = 'View all wedding bands'
      assign promo_heading = 'Signature Wedding Bands'
      assign promo_url = '/collections/wedding-bands'
      assign promo_image = 'category-wedding-bands.png'
      assign promo_style = ''
      assign promo_text = 'Plain metal, pavé and eternity bands, made to sit with the ring they are worn beside.'
      assign promo_actions = 'Shop wedding bands|/collections/wedding-bands,Shop eternity rings|/collections/eternity-rings' | split: ','
      assign promo_secondary = 'Eternity Rings|/collections/eternity-rings|featured-wedding-eternity.jpg|800|1020'
    when 'diamonds'
      comment
        Learn is the menu's own column of guide pages, so the shared Guides list is not asked for
        on top of it. The studio stays: the diamond-first route into it starts here.
      endcomment
      assign browse_columns = 'Lab-Grown Diamonds|Shop by Shape|shapes split|/collections/lab-grown-diamonds,Learn|Learn|' | split: ','
      assign promo_text = 'Choose a lab-grown stone and we will set it in the design you pick.'
      assign promo_actions = 'Start with a diamond|/collections/lab-grown-diamonds,Start with a setting|/pages/design-studio-builder' | split: ','
    when 'jewellery' or 'jewelry'
      comment
        A column per category, in the order a jewellery shopper reads them: Rings, Earrings,
        Necklaces, Bracelets, Men's. Each heading is the category's own collection and the names
        under it are its sub-ranges, which is the nesting the menu had on mobile but not here -
        the panel used to merge them all into one "Shop Jewellery" list, which read as a wall of
        names with no sign of where one category ended and the next began.

        Five columns, so they take "compact": the floor each one wraps at comes down far enough
        for all five to stay on one row beside the promo picture. Their names and order come
        from 'menu-static-items', so the panel and the mobile menu cannot drift apart.

        Neither Shape nor Stone is on the panel. Both are still groups in the navigation and
        still listed in 'menu-static-items' - Shape as the nine cuts, each with its drawing in
        assets - so the mobile menu and anything else that asks for them is unchanged; it is
        this panel that gives them no column. Putting "Shop by Shape|By Shape|shapes compact"
        or "Shop by Stone|Shop by Stone|inline" back into the list above is all it takes to
        return either. Keep a cut column's heading short: at the width a fifth of the row leaves
        it, "Shop by Shape" wraps onto a second line and takes its rule out of line with the
        four beside it, which is why the form above reads "By Shape".
      endcomment
      assign browse_columns = "Rings|Rings|compact|/collections/rings,Earrings|Earrings|compact|/collections/earrings,Necklaces|Necklaces|compact|/collections/necklaces,Bracelets|Bracelets|compact|/collections/bracelets,Men's|Men's|compact|/collections/mens-rings" | split: ','
      assign promo_heading = 'Best Sellers'
      assign promo_url = '/collections/best-sellers'
      assign promo_image = 'category-best-sellers.png'
      assign promo_width = 1122
      assign promo_height = 1402
      assign promo_style = ''
      assign promo_text = 'The pieces that leave the workshop most often, in earrings, necklaces and rings.'
      assign promo_actions = 'Shop best sellers|/collections/best-sellers,Shop new in|/collections/new-in' | split: ','
  endcase

  comment
    A menu running compact columns gets a tighter gap between them as well: five columns at the
    gap the two- and three-column menus use would not hold their row beside the promo picture at
    the narrow end, and the fifth dropped to a row of its own. Read off the columns rather than
    set per menu, so a menu that asks for compact columns gets the gap that goes with them.
  endcomment
  assign columns_tight = false
  for column in browse_columns
    assign column_probe = column | split: '|'
    if column_probe[2] contains 'compact'
      assign columns_tight = true
      break
    endif
  endfor
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  The menu's own handle rides on the page as a modifier, so a panel that wants something the
  others don't - Wedding's shorter heading rules and narrower columns - can be reached from CSS
  without a class per column. A menu with no rules of its own is unaffected by carrying it.
{%- endcomment -%}
<div
  class="menu-drawer-desktop__page menu-drawer-desktop__page--links menu-drawer-desktop__page--{{ parent_key }}"
  id="{{ drawer_id }}"
  data-menu-drawer-page
  hidden
>
  <section class="menu-drawer-desktop__half menu-drawer-desktop__half--browse">
    <div
      class="
        menu-drawer-desktop__columns
        {%- if columns_tight %} menu-drawer-desktop__columns--tight{% endif -%}
      "
    >
      {%- for column in browse_columns -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign column_parts = column | split: '|'
          assign column_group = column_parts[0]
          assign column_heading = column_parts[1] | default: column_parts[0]
          assign column_styles = column_parts[2] | split: ' '
          # Compared against '' rather than blank: a column with no heading url has no fourth
          # field at all, and `nil != blank` is not reliable across Liquid versions.
          assign column_url = column_parts[3] | default: ''

          capture column_source
            render 'menu-static-items', group: column_group, parent: link.title
          endcapture
          assign column_source = column_source | strip

          # Only the first section of a group is drawn: a second would need a heading of its own,
          # which the columns have no room for. Wedding lists its second section as a column.
          assign column_sections = column_source | split: ';;'
          assign column_parts_raw = column_sections[0] | split: '::'
          assign column_items_raw = column_parts_raw[0]
          if column_parts_raw.size > 1
            assign column_items_raw = column_parts_raw[1]
          endif
          assign column_items = column_items_raw | split: '~'

          # Which set of drawings the names in this column carry, if any. `render` takes no
          # variable for the snippet it renders, so each set is a branch of its own below.
          assign column_icons = ''
          if column_styles contains 'shapes'
            assign column_icons = 'shapes'
          elsif column_styles contains 'ring-styles'
            assign column_icons = 'ring-styles'
          elsif column_styles contains 'band-styles'
            assign column_icons = 'band-styles'
          elsif column_styles contains 'types'
            assign column_icons = 'types'
          elsif column_styles contains 'stones'
            assign column_icons = 'stones'
          endif
        -%}
        {%- if column_items.size > 0 -%}
          <div
            class="
              menu-drawer-desktop__column
              {%- for style in column_styles %} menu-drawer-desktop__column--{{ style }}{% endfor -%}
            "
          >
            {%- comment -%}
              Plain text, never a link. The heading labels the column; a shopper who wants the
              category itself takes the "View all" under the names, which is the one place a
              column's own destination is offered.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <h2 class="menu-drawer-desktop__column-heading">{{ column_heading | escape }}</h2>
            <ul class="menu-drawer-desktop__link-list" role="list">
              {%- for item in column_items -%}
                {%- liquid
                  assign item_parts = item | split: '|'
                  assign item_title = item_parts[0]
                  assign item_url = item_parts[1]
                  unless item_url contains '/'
                    assign item_url = item_url | prepend: '/collections/'
                  endunless
                  # `render` takes no filters in its arguments, so the icon's key is made here
                  assign item_key = item_title | handle
                -%}
                <li>
                  <a class="menu-drawer-desktop__link" href="{{ item_url }}">
                    {%- render 'menu-link-icon', icons: column_icons, key: item_key, prefix: 'menu-drawer-desktop__link-icon' -%}
                    <span class="menu-drawer-desktop__link-text">{{ item_title | escape }}</span>
                  </a>
                </li>
              {%- endfor -%}
            </ul>
            {%- if column_url != '' -%}
              {%- comment -%}
                The column's own way in to everything under it. The words stay short so they hold
                one line in a compact column, and the heading rides on the link as its label: five
                bare "View all"s read alike to anything that meets one out of its column.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              {%- assign column_cta_label = column_heading | prepend: 'View all ' -%}
              <a
                class="menu-drawer-desktop__column-cta"
                href="{{ column_url }}"
                aria-label="{{ column_cta_label | escape }}"
              >
                <span class="menu-drawer-desktop__link-text">View all</span>
                <span class="menu-drawer-desktop__column-cta-arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
              </a>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="menu-drawer-desktop__half menu-drawer-desktop__half--promo">
    <h2 class="menu-drawer-desktop__column-heading">
      <a class="menu-drawer-desktop__promo-heading-link" href="{{ promo_url }}">
        {{- promo_heading | escape -}}
      </a>
    </h2>

    {%- comment -%}
      A row, so that a menu carrying a second picture sets it beside the first under the one
      heading rule, and a menu carrying none is the row of one it was before.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="menu-drawer-desktop__promo-pair">
      <div
        class="
          menu-drawer-desktop__promo
          {%- if promo_style != '' %} menu-drawer-desktop__promo--{{ promo_style }}{% endif -%}
        "
      >
        <span class="menu-drawer-desktop__promo-media" aria-hidden="true">
          <img
            src="{% render 'image-source', file: promo_image, width: 900 %}"
            srcset="{% render 'image-source', file: promo_image, width: 600 %} 600w, {% render 'image-source', file: promo_image, width: 900 %} 900w"
            sizes="(min-width: 1200px) 34vw, 30vw"
            alt=""
            width="{{ promo_width }}"
            height="{{ promo_height }}"
            loading="lazy"
          >
        </span>
        <div class="menu-drawer-desktop__promo-overlay">
          <p class="menu-drawer-desktop__promo-text">{{ promo_text | escape }}</p>
          <div class="menu-drawer-desktop__promo-actions">
            {%- for action in promo_actions -%}
              {%- assign action_parts = action | split: '|' -%}
              <a
                class="menu-drawer-desktop__button menu-drawer-desktop__button--on-image"
                href="{{ action_parts[1] }}"
              >{{ action_parts[0] | escape }}</a>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      {%- comment -%}
        The second picture, where a menu asks for one. A link rather than a panel of its own:
        the picture beside it carries the copy and the two buttons, and this is one more way in,
        so the whole tile is the hit area and the name over its foot is the only word on it.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if promo_secondary != '' -%}
        {%- assign secondary_parts = promo_secondary | split: '|' -%}
        <a
          class="menu-drawer-desktop__promo menu-drawer-desktop__promo--secondary"
          href="{{ secondary_parts[1] }}"
        >
          <span class="menu-drawer-desktop__promo-media" aria-hidden="true">
            <img
              src="{% render 'image-source', file: secondary_parts[2], width: 700 %}"
              srcset="{% render 'image-source', file: secondary_parts[2], width: 450 %} 450w, {% render 'image-source', file: secondary_parts[2], width: 700 %} 700w"
              sizes="(min-width: 1400px) 22vw, 30vw"
              alt=""
              width="{{ secondary_parts[3] }}"
              height="{{ secondary_parts[4] }}"
              loading="lazy"
            >
          </span>
          <span class="menu-drawer-desktop__promo-overlay">
            {%- comment -%}
              Spans, not a link: the whole tile is already the anchor. They carry the promo's
              button classes so this reads as the third button in the row rather than a label of
              its own kind - see 'menu-drawer-desktop__promo-label' in the stylesheet.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <span class="
              menu-drawer-desktop__button
              menu-drawer-desktop__button--on-image
              menu-drawer-desktop__promo-label
            ">{{ secondary_parts[0] | escape }}</span>
          </span>
        </a>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="menu-drawer-desktop__links-footer">
    {%- if link.url != blank -%}
      <a class="menu-drawer-desktop__footer-cta" href="{{ link.url }}">
        <span class="menu-drawer-desktop__link-text">{{ view_all_label | escape }}</span>
        <span class="menu-drawer-desktop__footer-arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
      </a>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</div>
